sweet-spi-defer-unmask (lowclk 2026-11-13, design notes: lowclk irq study-check W3 + s.4; shared SPI glue for the Wi-Fi INTx doorbell of patch 0347, no behaviour change for the GPU): pexpert/arm/pe_fiq.c, on top of patch 0272.
(1) SWEET_SPI_SLOTS 4 -> 8 [the GPU attaches 2: INTID 452, 453]. (2) A handler may return SWEET_SPI_DEFER (2) = "handled, mask me until my thread calls sweet_spi_unmask": the dispatcher writes the same GICD_ICENABLER bit as the safety net but counts it in sweet_spi_deferred, not in
sweet_spi_unhandled; 0 and every other non-zero value behave exactly as before [read 0272 sm_isr returns 0 or 1 only]. (3) sweet_spi_attach_off(): attach + configure (disable, clear pending/active, Group 1, priority 0xA0, level, route to the boot CPU) and leave the SPI DISABLED
(no ISENABLER write); sweet_spi_attach() is now sweet_spi_attach_x(..., enable = 1), the same GICD accesses in the same order as in 0272 (the only change is the wrapper). (4) sweet_spi_enable() (first enable) and sweet_spi_unmask() (re-enable after a mask): one ISENABLER write of the INTID's own bit,
RWP wait, read-back; both refuse an INTID with no attached handler (22). Hardware access of this patch: none by itself (no caller in this patch); the callers are 0347 (INTID 541, boot-arg sweetwifiirq=1) and the GPU, whose accesses are unchanged. Host test: tools/test_spi_glue.py compiles the table logic.
